[#:seon.task{:name "carried-receipt-hangs-on-cyclic-cause-chain"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`seon.fault/carried-receipt` never returns on a cyclic cause chain and cannot be cancelled (a probe held one core at 99% for ~7 minutes); seon.render.value/floor walks the same chain safely. Walk causes with a visited set at the one normalization owner."
             :must-read #{seon.fault/carried-receipt}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/docs-exploration-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "fault-write-bound-is-wall-clock-under-contention"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`seon.fault-test/a-fault-stores-the-whole-fault-and-wakes-the-responsible-agent` asserts (< elapsed-ms 1000.0) for one synchronous fault write; serial it passes, at six concurrent test requests it measured 1,026 and 1,040 ms (CPU and store I/O contention; transact-call averaged 149 ms against 95 ms serial). Done when the write's cost is proportional to the fault (measure where the ~1 s goes) and the bound holds under the declared test admission bound."
             :must-read #{seon.fault/fault!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/test-agents-concurrency-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "log-lines-print-values-outside-the-printer"
             :kind :namespace
             :intent "Seon writes log, stderr and stdout lines that print values outside the value printer (fault print-unrecorded!, boot memory pressure, datahike-log! events, fs deletion reports, web page and request faults, test runner failure reports) and log-only warnings with no delivered fault (projection fallback, declaration population fallback, low disk space). CLAUDE.md: recording without delivery, a log line or a panic alone, is a defect; owner 2026-10-07: no bulk in logs. Inventory class log, 30 sites: test/runner.clj 5, cluster.clj 4, cluster/boot.clj 3, cluster/store.clj 3, render/web.clj 3, schema.clj 3, script/operator.clj 2, db.clj 2, fault.clj 2, fs.clj 2, sci/eval.clj 1 (17 grow with input, 13 fixed text). Done when each is a recorded fault delivered as data (the line, if any, names the fault id and nothing printed from a value), and seon.fault-test asserts a fault whose evidence prints over 1 MB writes no stderr line longer than one bounded sentence."
             :must-read #{seon.fault/print-unrecorded! seon.cluster.store/datahike-log! seon.fs/log-deletion!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/task-census/evidence/no-print-hash--print-sites.tsv" "docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/task-census/evidence/no-print-hash--notes.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name
            "a-delivered-fault-names-the-normalizer-not-its-boundary",
            :kind :function,
            :intent
            "`seon.fault/fault!` with context {`:seon.error/layer` :seon.flow/proc `:seon.error/operation` seon.flow/probe} stores the error entity with that layer and operation, but the occurrence copies the prepared source's diagnostic attributes (`:seon.error/layer` :seon.error/normalization, `:seon.error/operation` the blamed producer `seon.sci.kernel/adopt-arm`), and `seon.error/latest-fact` merges the occurrence over the entity, so the reply's :errors entry and every latest-fact reader name the normalizer, not the boundary that recorded it. Reproduce: the fault! call above; :errors showed `:seon.error/layer` :seon.error/normalization, `:seon.error/operation` `seon.sci.kernel/adopt-arm` while (`seon.db/pull` db [`:seon.error/operation` `:seon.error/layer`] [`:seon.error/signature` s]) answered seon.flow/probe / :seon.flow/proc. Correct: the boundary's layer and operation reach the prepared observation (prepare's boundary-layer/boundary-operation) so entity and occurrence agree. Proof: fault! with an explicit layer reads that layer back from latest-fact.",
            :must-read
            #{seon.error/commit-call
              seon.error/latest-fact
              seon.fault/record!}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-fault-on-a-branch-is-recorded-once-there-and-counted-on-main-at-the-next-auto-merge"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Phase U7 of hybrid-push.md (replaces hybrid-agent-world.md's P5; after U0 and U1). `seon.error.occurrence/occurrence` is a :seon.cluster entity, so `seon.fault/record!` writes ONE transaction on the world's own connection and its second write (the cluster-branch copy naming the origin) is deleted; on every hit it adds the recording world's attempt to :seon.error.occurrence/attempts, the ownership fact `seon.cluster.squash/auto-merge-tx` selects by. The next auto-merge of its merge request carries the occurrence onto main: :seon.error.occurrence/count by :add (theirs minus the merged base), :seon.error.occurrence/last-at by :max; :seon.error.occurrence/evaluation stays a :seon.cluster.eval/id value (`:seon.db/reference-to`), so no ref dangles on main. Proof: this test (one transaction on the branch; after the auto-merge main holds the signature with count 1 and the attempt in attempts; a second attempt's same signature makes 2, never an overwrite; a repeat adds nothing; an occurrence naming no attempt of this branch waits in the merge request). Files: src/seon/fault.clj, test/seon/fault_test.clj."
             :must-read #{seon.fault/record! seon.fault/fault! seon.turn.world/record-fault}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/hybrid-push.md" "docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-11/hybrid-agent-world.md"}}]
